  "aiContextParagraph": "Former Brazilian President Jair Bolsonaro was admitted to the DF Star hospital in Brasilia on November 20, 2026, following complaints of severe abdominal pain. Medical bulletins confirmed he is receiving treatment for an intestinal obstruction and a pneumonia diagnosis. He was initially moved to the intensive care unit for specialized monitoring. Recent updates from medical staff on November 24 indicate a slight clinical improvement in his condition, and he has begun antibiotic therapy. Despite these signs of progress and previous reports from his family describing an endoscopy result as positive, the hospital has not provided a specific timeline for his release. Bolsonaro remains hospitalized while staff continue to manage his recovery from the dual health issues reported by multiple outlets. His condition is currently characterized as stable as he continues his medical treatment.",
